meta {
  name: List Page/Form Org Mappings
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/page-org-map?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  Lists every Page/Form -> org mapping for the ADMINISTERED tenant — the one
  named by ?tenant_id=, which is what the lookup-admin navbar switcher sends.
  Requires super_admin (platform rank 1000); every other caller gets 403,
  including on this read, which had no rank gate at all before.

  tenant_id is required and is NOT defaulted to the caller's own tenant.
  Platform staff belong to a different tenant than the one they administer, so
  the previous behaviour — taking tenant_id from the caller's gateway-injected
  headers — listed their own tenant's mappings, i.e. none.

  Scoping is enforced in the database, not by a WHERE clause: the query runs
  under withTenantConfigTx with app.current_tenant_id pinned to tenant_id, and
  ext.meta_page_form_org_map's admin_tenant_config_policy fences the rows.

  Tenant-scoping regression checks:
    * omit tenant_id            -> 422 (validation)
    * tenant_id = a bogus uuid  -> 404 Tenant not found
    * tenant_id = tenant B      -> only tenant B's rows, never tenant A's
}
